> zmat det [[1,0,0,0,0],[2,3,0,0,0],[0,0,5,0,0],[0,0,0,7,0],[1,0,0,0,11]]
det = 1155
  how: Bareiss fraction-free elimination
  check: Gaussian elimination over Q gives 1155
> zmat rank [[1,2,3],[2,4,6],[0,0,0]]
rank = 1
  how: Bareiss fraction-free elimination
  check: the Smith form has 1 nonzero invariant factors
> zmat kernel [[1,2],[2,4]]
kernel of the 2x2 matrix over Z: rank 1
  basis (columns): [[2], [-1]]
  how: U A^T = H (Hermite); the rows of U past the rank; a saturated basis (Z^2 / ker is torsion free)
  check: A K = 0
> zmat image [[1,2],[3,4]]
image of the 2x2 matrix (the lattice of its columns): rank 2
  basis (columns, Hermite form): [[1, 0], [1, 2]]
  index / quotient: Z^2 / image = Z/2
  check: each column of A lies in the lattice and each basis vector in the column span: verified
> snf [[2,4,0],[0,6,0],[0,0,12]]
Smith normal form of the 3x3 matrix: diag(2, 6, 12), rank 3
  D: [[2, 0, 0], [0, 6, 0], [0, 0, 12]]
  U: [[1, 0, 0], [0, 1, 0], [0, 0, 1]]
  V: [[1, -2, 0], [0, 1, 0], [0, 0, 1]]
  U^-1: [[1, 0, 0], [0, 1, 0], [0, 0, 1]]
  V^-1: [[1, 2, 0], [0, 1, 0], [0, 0, 1]]
  cokernel: Z^3 / (columns) = Z/2 + Z/6 + Z/12
  check: U A V = D, U U^-1 = I and V V^-1 = I (unimodular), d_i | d_(i+1): verified
> hnf [[2,4,0],[0,6,0],[0,0,12]]
Hermite normal form (rows) of the 3x3 matrix: rank 3
  H: [[2, 4, 0], [0, 6, 0], [0, 0, 12]]
  U: [[1, 0, 0], [0, 1, 0], [0, 0, 1]]
  check: U A = H, det U = +-1, H in echelon form with positive pivots and reduced entries above them: verified
> zmat solve [[2,0],[0,2]], [[4],[6]]
x = [[2], [3]]
  check: A x = b
> zmat solve [[1,2],[2,4]], [[3],[6]]
x = [[3], [0]]
  general solution: x + K t, K = [[2], [-1]]
  check: A x = b
